# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — ProcessQueue input parity
# Recorded: 2026-10-22 23:39:17 UTC
# Code revision: 267173dd

## Compatibility finding

Pinned Java 5.5.1 `ProcessQueue.putMessage` parses the last message's
`MAX_OFFSET` only after inserting messages and setting the dispatch flag. An
invalid or overflowing value raises `NumberFormatException` without rolling
back those state changes. Rust now returns
`ProcessQueueError::InvalidMaxOffset` after preserving the same queue state.
The subsequent valid insertion does not request another dispatch. Java also
sets `lastPullTimestamp` at the pull-request boundary, not in `putMessage`;
Rust owner flow now has the same timestamp ownership.

The invoked `ConsumerFacadeApiFixtures` comparison covers the Java exception
class, queue counts/bytes/tree, following dispatch result, and preservation of
a caller-set last-pull timestamp. Fixture SHA-256:
`a334ff119c014259676917531ce4032160b10209cdac027d9963d2c1327d5d6a`.

